{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, one pass: a self-loop is noticed while the search reads the vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successors.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The components are those of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stronglyConnectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":" without the trivial ones, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order, a reverse topological order: every path between two of them goes from a later"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one to an earlier one. Each lists its vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. Empty exactly when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph is acyclic. Each is a slice of one shared array, as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attractingComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":", so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices do not start at 0."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":", so one sort by that vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position puts the components in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, O(C log C) for C components. On a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", where positions are insertion order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","    .sorted { graph.vertexPosition(of: $0.first!) < graph.vertexPosition(of: $1.first!) }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(V + E)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nontrivial strongly connected components: the ones that contain a cycle, which are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components of two or more vertices and the single vertices with a self-loop. A vertex is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one exactly when it lies on a cycle, and two vertices share one exactly when a cycle passes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through both."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ArraySlice","preciseIdentifier":"s:s10ArraySliceV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">]"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"title":"nontrivialStronglyConnectedComponents()","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com